module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.AdicMilnorCompletionComparison
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.LocalizationCompletionFiniteType

/-!
# The restriction of the pinned comparison to a slice is the slice's own pinned comparison

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` a sheaf of ideals of finite type, `L` derived complete
along `ℐ` and `u : K ⟶ L`. `AdicQuotientComparisonPinned.lean` attaches to `u` the comparison

`c = pinnedAdicComparison X I hL u : K^∧ ⟶ L`,

the unique map out of the derived completion restricting to `u` along the completion unit. This
file proves that `c` restricts to the corresponding map on every slice: under the isomorphism
`(K|_U)^∧ ≅ K^∧|_U` of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F], `c|_U` is the pinned comparison of `u|_U` on
`(𝒞/U, 𝒪_U)` along `ℐ|_U`.

That is the first of the two things the hypothesis `hloc` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_coversTop`
asks for: it removes the global map from that hypothesis, leaving a statement formulated entirely
inside the slice.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionRestrictIso_hom_app_comp_map_pinnedAdicComparison`
  — the identification. The proof is one application of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.eq_pinnedAdicComparison`: the slice's completion unit followed by
  the restricted map is `u|_U`, by [Stacks, Tag 0A0F]'s compatibility of the two completion units
  (`derivedCompletionUnit_app_comp_derivedCompletionRestrictIso_hom_app`) and the defining
  property of `c`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_map_pinnedAdicComparison_of_isIso_slice` — hence `c|_U` is
  invertible as soon as the slice's own pinned comparison is.
* `RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_coversTop_slice`
  — part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] for an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪)` with the chart hypothesis in
  the purely slice-local form.

## What this does not settle, and where the obstruction is

The remaining hypothesis is `IsIso (pinnedAdicComparison (𝒞/U, 𝒪_U) (ℐ|_U) (u|_U))`, and on a
chart where `ℐ|_U` is generated by finitely many sections it is **not** a consequence of the
per-chart part (1) that the library has. What the chart supplies is
`Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimitWithProjections_adicReductionTower_generatedIdealSheaf`:
`(K|_U)^∧` is a derived limit of the restricted tower *through the canonical factorizations of
[Stacks, Tag 0CQH]*. The restriction `L|_U` of the named `R lim` is a derived limit of the same
tower through the restricted projections, and the pinned comparison matches the two families of
projections (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pinnedAdicComparison_comp`). But matching projections
does not make a comparison invertible: the third square of the morphism of Milnor triangles is
undetermined, the indeterminacy being `Hom((K|_U)^∧, (∏ₙ K|_U ⊗^𝐋 𝒪_U/(ℐ|_U)ⁿ⁺¹)⟦-1⟧)`. That is
exactly the group that `Stacks.Algebraization.hom_ext_of_comp_proj` of
`Completion/AdicQuotientCanonicalComparison.lean` makes vanish from `IsLE 0` on the source and
`IsGE 0` on the terms of the tower, and whose non-vanishing that file's
`Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_of_isDerivedLimitWithProjections_of_comp_proj` records as making the
projection-matching statement false in general.

So the input part (1) at an arbitrary `K` still waits on is a replacement for those two degree
bounds — or a model-level construction on the chart identifying the Čech completion with the
Milnor fibre *compatibly with the two augmentations out of `K`*, which is what the universal
property cannot supply and what the derived-category statements above do not contain.

## The obstruction restated as a vanishing, and why the compatibility is free in the source

`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_pinnedAdicComparison_of_leftOrthogonal_cone` of
`AdicComparisonConeOrthogonality.lean` replaces the hypothesis above by one about a single
object and **no degree bound at all**: the pinned comparison at `u` is invertible as soon as
every map from the cone of `u` into a derived-complete object is zero, equivalently as soon as
the derived completion of that cone vanishes. The converse is
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.leftOrthogonal_cone_unit` of
`Completion/ReflectionAlongTriangulatedFunctor.lean`, so this is the same open input in a
different shape, not a weaker one.

**The Koszul route through that criterion is circular**; the module documentation of
`AdicComparisonConeOrthogonality.lean` carries the computation. On a chart [Stacks, Tag 0A0E]
presents the Čech completion of *any* object as `R lim (- ⊗^𝐋 (Kⁿ)^∨)` with no hypothesis at all
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion`
of `KoszulPerfectDual.lean`), and a derived limit is zero once the Milnor difference map of its
tower is invertible (`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit.isZero_of_isIso_difference`),
which on a tower of zero objects it is. So the criterion does follow from the per-term vanishing
`cone(u|_U) ⊗^𝐋 (Kⁿ)^∨ = 0`, with no derived-limit comparison and no third square to determine.
But that per-term vanishing is *equivalent* to the invertibility it would prove. Writing
`u = η ≫ c`, the octahedral triangle `cone(η) ⟶ cone(u) ⟶ cone(c)` together with the vanishing
of `cone(η) ⊗^𝐋 (Kⁿ)^∨` — which is true, and non-circularly, because `cone(η)` is `R𝑆heafHom`
out of the non-extended Čech complex, on each of whose terms some `f_i` acts invertibly, while
`(Kⁿ)^∨` is an iterated cone of the `f_i^{n+1}` — reduces it to a statement about `cone(c)`;
and `cone(c)` is derived complete, where the criterion says only that the object vanishes
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.leftOrthogonal_iff_isZero_of_isDerivedComplete`). The mechanism
that is available cancels exactly the part that was free.

**Why the augmentation compatibility the paragraph above asks for is automatic in the source,
and what it would take here.** On the chart the completion is
`R𝑆heafHom(Č(f), -)` (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor`) and `Č(f)` is the
*honest* colimit of the Koszul complexes
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isColimitKoszulCechComplexCocone` of `KoszulCechColimit.lean`),
so against a complex of injectives `𝓗om(Č(f), -)` is the **kernel** of the Milnor difference map
on `∏ₙ 𝓗om(Kⁿ, -)` rather than merely its homotopy kernel. A map into a kernel is determined by
its composite with the kernel inclusion, which is a monomorphism, so there the comparison with
the Milnor fibre carries the completion unit to the Milnor augmentation with nothing to check:
that, and not any property of the derived category, is what makes the source's identification
unit-compatible. Reproducing it needs four things the library does not have: the telescope short
exact sequence `0 ⟶ ⊕ₙ Kⁿ ⟶ ⊕ₙ Kⁿ ⟶ Č(f) ⟶ 0` of complexes; exactness of `𝓗om(-, J)` on it for
`J` a complex of injectives; the quasi-isomorphism from `Stacks.MilnorTower.milnorObj` of a
degreewise-surjective difference map onto its kernel; and `IsIso` of
`Stacks.MilnorTower.mappingCoconeMap` at a map of towers with
`NoetherianAdicCompletion.HasEventualInverses` — the last of which is proved, privately and for
the other Milnor functor, as `isIso_milnorMap_of_proIso` of
`Homology/DerivedComplete/NoetherianCompletePrincipalIdeal.lean`. The augmentation half is
already available at model level and costs nothing:
`Stacks.MilnorTower.TowerAugmentation.augmentationMap_naturality` of
`CategoryTheory/Triangulated/MilnorFibreTower.lean`.

The first three of those four are needed only to identify the Čech side of the comparison. They
are **not** needed if the tower compared against the adic tower is the *constant* tower, whose
Milnor fibre is already identified with its value by `constantTower_augmentation_quasiIso` of
`Homology/DerivedComplete/AdicDerivedCompletionKoszul.lean`, and whose augmentation
compatibility is exactly what `augmentationMap_naturality` supplies. That variant needs only the
fourth, together with `NoetherianAdicCompletion.HasEventualInverses` for the augmentation of the
constant tower at `(Kⁿ)^∨` — which holds. The proof, and the single input it rests on that this
library lacks, are recorded in the module documentation of
`DerivedCompletionRinged/AdicComparisonConeOrthogonality.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CQH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CQH)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_ringCat

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
  [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType] (U : X.C)
  {K L : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}

/-- **The pinned comparison restricts to the slice's own pinned comparison.** Under the
isomorphism `(K|_U)^∧ ≅ K^∧|_U` of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F], the restriction of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pinnedAdicComparison` at `u : K ⟶ L` is the pinned comparison of
`u|_U` on the slice along `ℐ|_U`.

Nothing is chosen on either side, so this is a computation with the defining properties: the
slice's completion unit followed by the restriction of `c` is the restriction of the global unit
followed by `c`, which is `u`. -/
theorem derivedCompletionRestrictIso_hom_app_comp_map_pinnedAdicComparison
    (hL : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I L)
    (hL' : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} (X.over U) (overIdeal I U)
      ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          U).mapDerivedCategory.obj L))
    (u : K ⟶ L) :
    (derivedCompletionRestrictIso X I U).hom.app K ≫
        (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
            U).mapDerivedCategory.map
          (pinnedAdicComparison X I hL u) =
      pinnedAdicComparison (X.over U) (overIdeal I U) hL'
        ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
            U).mapDerivedCategory.map u) := by
  refine eq_pinnedAdicComparison (X.over U) (overIdeal I U) hL' _ ?_
  refine (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans ?_
  refine (eq_whisker
    (derivedCompletionUnit_app_comp_derivedCompletionRestrictIso_hom_app X I U K) _).trans ?_
  refine ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
    U).mapDerivedCategory.map_comp _ _).symm.trans ?_
  exact congrArg
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
        U).mapDerivedCategory.map (derivedCompletionUnit_comp_pinnedAdicComparison X I hL u)

/-- **The restriction of the pinned comparison is invertible as soon as the slice's own pinned
comparison is.** Immediate from
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionRestrictIso_hom_app_comp_map_pinnedAdicComparison`,
the first factor there being an isomorphism by [Stacks, Tag 0A0F]. -/
theorem isIso_map_pinnedAdicComparison_of_isIso_slice
    (hL : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I L)
    (hL' : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} (X.over U) (overIdeal I U)
      ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          U).mapDerivedCategory.obj L))
    (u : K ⟶ L)
    (h : IsIso (pinnedAdicComparison (X.over U) (overIdeal I U) hL'
      ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          U).mapDerivedCategory.map u))) :
    IsIso ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
        U).mapDerivedCategory.map (pinnedAdicComparison X I hL u)) := by
  have : IsIso ((derivedCompletionRestrictIso X I U).hom.app K) := inferInstance
  have : IsIso ((derivedCompletionRestrictIso X I U).hom.app K ≫
      (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          U).mapDerivedCategory.map (pinnedAdicComparison X I hL u)) := by
    rw [derivedCompletionRestrictIso_hom_app_comp_map_pinnedAdicComparison X I U hL hL' u]
    exact h
  exact IsIso.of_isIso_comp_left ((derivedCompletionRestrictIso X I U).hom.app K) _

section Locality

variable [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : X.C, HasWeakSheafify (X.J.over V) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : X.C, (X.J.over V).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over V) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- **Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] for an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪)`, with the chart hypothesis
in slice-local form.** Let `V : ι → 𝒞` cover the final object of the site. If on the slice over
each `V i` the pinned comparison of the restricted named map
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.kInjectiveAdicComparison` is invertible, then the derived completion
of `K` is a derived limit of the tower `n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹`.

This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_coversTop`
with its hypothesis rewritten by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_map_pinnedAdicComparison_of_isIso_slice`, so that no global
map appears in it. The remaining hypothesis is still open; the module documentation says where
the obstruction to it is and what it is a group of.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached: this is a conditional statement and proves no assertion of
the tag. -/
theorem isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_coversTop_slice
    (Kt : CochainComplex (Modules X) ℤ) (hKt : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsKFlat X.O Kt)
    (e : DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kt ≅ K)
    {ι : Type*} {V : ι → X.C} (hV : X.J.CoversTop V)
    (hL' : ∀ i, IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} (X.over (V i)) (overIdeal I (V i))
      ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          (V i)).mapDerivedCategory.obj (kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj X I Kt)))
    (hloc : ∀ i, IsIso (pinnedAdicComparison (X.over (V i)) (overIdeal I (V i)) (hL' i)
      ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          (V i)).mapDerivedCategory.map (kInjectiveAdicComparison X I Kt)))) :
    IsDerivedLimit (adicReductionTower X I K) ((derivedCompletion X I).obj K) :=
  isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_coversTop X I Kt hKt e hV fun i =>
    isIso_map_pinnedAdicComparison_of_isIso_slice X I (V i)
      (isDerivedComplete_kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj X I Kt hKt) (hL' i)
      (kInjectiveAdicComparison X I Kt) (hloc i)

end Locality

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
